      "source_function": "accept_completion_025720",
      "source_fragment": "void accept_completion_025720(Error error, Session* session, ServerBackend& server, Scheduling& scheduling) {\n    if (error.value == 0) session->start_025720();\n    else scheduling.log_error(\"accept\",error);\n    server.async_accept_021b00();\n}",
      "previous_behavior": "Any non-stop accept completion error closed listener and set stopping=true/ready=false.",
      "source_behavior": "Log accept error, then async_accept again.",
      "change": "Remove only terminal close/stopping/return from accept-completion error branch. Explicit stop, rearm allocation failure and dispatcher failure retain their prior terminal handling.",
      "why_previous_change_occurred": "Owned callback collapsed accept completion errors into a terminal service state. This is visible in source; historical reason was not recorded. Upstream Asio does not require this branch.",
      "test": "Existing real TCP Asio integration extended with Linux test-executable-only accept syscall boundary fault: three EMFILE completions, same listener/port, normal response, later client, explicit stop. Windows boundary NOT_RUN.",
      "non_goals": [
        "no retry budget/backoff/new config selector",
        "no dependency or production fault-injection API",
        "no phase/thread/provider/handler-pool changes"
      ]
    }
  },
